@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{org-linear-extras.el} extends @samp{org-linear} with a model-backed merge of description edits. In org-linear's in-place layout@comma{} Org is the primary copy of a task@comma{} and a description edited in Linear normally replaces the heading's body. When the body holds markup that Markdown cannot carry@comma{} such as a source block's header arguments@comma{} that replacement would lose it@comma{} so org-linear asks @code{org-linear-merge-body-function} to merge the edit instead. This package supplies such a function@comma{} which asks a model through @samp{gptel}.

@node Merging description edits
@chapter Merging description edits

@findex org-linear-extras-merge-body
@code{org-linear-extras-merge-body} is meant as the value of @code{org-linear-merge-body-function}. It sends the model the current Org body@comma{} the Markdown the body was last converted to and Linear's new Markdown@comma{} and asks for the Org body that applies the edit while keeping the Org-only markup of the passages that did not change. It passes the reply to org-linear@comma{} stripped of any code fence around it@comma{} or @samp{nil} if the request failed. org-linear uses the reply only if it converts to Linear's text@comma{} so a wrong merge leaves both sides as they were and is retried at the next sync.

@vindex org-linear-extras-merge-backend
@vindex org-linear-extras-merge-model
@code{org-linear-extras-merge-backend} names the gptel backend that answers@comma{} @samp{"Claude"} by default@comma{} and @code{org-linear-extras-merge-model} the model@comma{} or @samp{nil} for @code{gptel-model}. The request uses no tools and no gptel context.

@vindex org-linear-extras-merge-system
The instructions the model gets are in @code{org-linear-extras-merge-system}.

